                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Son / Sun — Say It Out Loud", body: "Say these out loud:\n\n\"The Son of God.\"\n\"The Sun of God.\"\n\nThey're phonetically identical in English.\n\nNow, English didn't exist when Christianity was founded. So this isn't proof of a deliberate ancient code. But here's what IS interesting:\n\nIn Latin (the language of the Roman Church that formalized Christianity):\n• Sol = Sun\n• Filius = Son\n\nDifferent words. But the Roman solar deity was SOL INVICTUS — the Unconquered Sun. And Constantine, the emperor who made Christianity the state religion in 313 AD, was a worshiper of Sol Invictus until his deathbed.\n\nThe coin Constantine minted AFTER his supposed conversion still showed Sol Invictus on one side and the Christian chi-rho on the other. He wasn't choosing between the sun god and Jesus. He was MERGING them.\n\nEvery attribute of Sol Invictus was transferred to Christ:\n• Born December 25th (Sol's birthday, Dies Natalis Solis Invicti)\n• Described as \"the light of the world\"\n• Depicted with a radiant halo\n• Worshiped on SUNday (Sol's day, not the Jewish Sabbath of Saturday)\n• Church orientation facing east (toward the rising Sol)\n\nThe English phonetic overlap of Son/Sun may be coincidental. But the THEOLOGICAL overlap between the Sun God and the Son of God is historically documented, institutionally implemented, and architecturally encoded.\n\nThe Roman Empire didn't convert to Christianity. Christianity was converted to Roman solar theology. And the evidence is on every church wall, in every liturgical calendar, and in the language itself."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "More Encoded Language", body: "Once you start seeing it, it's everywhere:\n\nGOSPEL: The \"good news\" — but in Old English, God = good, and spell = story/news. \"God's spell.\" A spell cast by God. Or a story ABOUT God that works like a spell on your mind.\n\nHOLY / HALO: Both from the same Proto-Germanic root hailag, meaning \"whole, sacred, inviolable.\" The halo literally means \"holy\" — the sun disk IS holiness, in the language itself.\n\nSUNDAY: Christians worship on Sunday. Not Saturday (the Jewish Sabbath). Not any other day. SUN-day. The day of the Sun. Emperor Constantine officially decreed in 321 AD that Sunday would be the day of rest — honoring Sol, the sun. Christianity adopted it wholesale.\n\nCHURCH: From the Greek kyriakon — \"of the Lord.\" But which Lord? In solar theology, the Lord IS the Sun — the Lord of Light, the ruler of the heavens, the source of all life.\n\nMONSTRANCE: From Latin monstrare — \"to show.\" The golden sun-ray vessel SHOWS you the truth. The sun. With a white circle (host/wafer) at its center. It literally demonstrates solar worship while calling it communion.\n\nCORONA: Crown. The sun's corona = its crown of rays. The \"crown of thorns\" = the corona. The coronation of kings = receiving the sun's crown. Every king claims the sun's authority.\n\nORIENT / ORIENTATION: From Latin oriens — \"rising\" (as in the sun rising in the east). To be oriented = to face the sunrise. Churches are oriented. Your entire sense of direction is based on the sun.\n\nILLUMINATION: From Latin illuminare — \"to light up.\" Spiritual illumination = becoming filled with light. Manuscript illumination = gold leaf that catches light. The ILLUMINATI = \"the illuminated ones\" — those who carry the sun's light.\n\nThey embedded it in every word. Every symbol. Every building. Every calendar date. Every piece of art.\n\nAnd they never. Said. A word."),
